WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:05.840
Whether you are a fan from way back, or just got&nbsp;
into the series when it was added to HBO Max,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:10.400
The Big Bang Theory remains one of the most&nbsp;
binge-worthy sitcoms in recent memory. With&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:17.280
a story that runs 12 seasons and 279 episodes,&nbsp;
the series makes for many hours of enjoyment,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:22.480
as well as plenty of opportunities to spot&nbsp;
potential plot holes and continuity errors.

00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:27.120
That's to be expected with any long-running&nbsp;
series, though, and spotting gaps in logic,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:32.160
or very specific errors, can even add an&nbsp;
extra level of enjoyment to a rewatch.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:36.480
Fans of The Big Bang Theory certainly seem&nbsp;
to think so, as they often take to Reddit to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:41.440
share the plot holes they uncover deep in the&nbsp;
show's history. Unraveling how these mess-ups&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.440 --> 00:00:46.480
affect the rest of the series, then, also adds&nbsp;
to the fun of seeking them out. One error,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:51.360
recently uncovered by eagle-eyed Redditors,&nbsp;
carries big implications for the backstory of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:56.320
Sheldon Cooper, not only on The Big Bang Theory,&nbsp;
but also the prequel series, Young Sheldon.

00:00:56.320 --> 00:01:01.280
There's an issue with Sheldon's age, and it isn't&nbsp;
that the show hasn't told us when he was born.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.280 --> 00:01:06.480
Rather, the problem is that the show tells us when&nbsp;
Sheldon was born, but later contradicts that date.

00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:12.240
It was referenced multiple times that Sheldon and&nbsp;
his twin sister Missy were born on February 26,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:16.000
1980. However, as Reddit user dgiannak discovered,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:21.440
the math of Sheldon's various life accomplishments&nbsp;
doesn't quite add up, if one examines Sheldon's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.440 --> 00:01:26.000
own accounting of his past in the first&nbsp;
season episode, "The Luminous Fish Effect."

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:31.200
After he gets fired from his job, Sheldon declares&nbsp;
he's not interested in getting it back, saying,

00:01:31.840 --> 00:01:35.840
"I've spent the past three and a half years&nbsp;
staring at grease boards full of equations.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.840 --> 00:01:38.880
Before that, I spent four years&nbsp;
working on my thesis. Before that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.880 --> 00:01:41.520
I was in college, and before&nbsp;
that, I was in the fifth grade."

00:01:42.160 --> 00:01:47.680
Now, another established fact is that Sheldon,&nbsp;
being the difficult genius he is, started college&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.680 --> 00:01:53.840
when he was eleven years old, a major plot point&nbsp;
in Young Sheldon. However, dgiannak notes that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.840 --> 00:01:59.280
when that timeline is added up — four years for&nbsp;
college, four for his PhD thesis, and three and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.280 --> 00:02:04.480
a half working before the beginning of the series&nbsp;
— that puts his age in "The Luminous Fish Effect"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.480 --> 00:02:10.800
at only 22. That's about five years shy of how&nbsp;
old he should be, at that point, which is 27.

00:02:10.800 --> 00:02:15.280
This timeline fumble is likely nothing&nbsp;
more than the result of a mistake in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.280 --> 00:02:19.200
script. But it's also not the first time&nbsp;
the show has had trouble pinning down&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:24.400
exactly when Sheldon was born. The show&nbsp;
also goofed on Sheldon's astrological sign.

00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:28.480
Whether or not you believe that someone's&nbsp;
astrological sign has any correlation to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.480 --> 00:02:33.840
their personality, western astrology does work&nbsp;
off of a specific set of dates to categorize&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:39.120
people into one of twelve specific signs.&nbsp;
However, in the case of The Big Bang Theory,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.120 --> 00:02:44.640
the lines between someone's actual birthday and&nbsp;
their sign occasionally gets blurred. For example,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:47.280
in the season one episode, "The Peanut Reaction,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.280 --> 00:02:51.760
Penny is talking with Sheldon and Leonard&nbsp;
about the group's various zodiac signs.

00:02:51.760 --> 00:02:52.320
She says,

00:02:53.040 --> 00:02:56.960
"I was gonna do everybody's until Sheldon&nbsp;
went on one of his typical psychotic rants."

00:02:56.960 --> 00:03:01.760
After Sheldon repeats his rant against the&nbsp;
legitimacy of astrology, Penny responds,

00:03:01.760 --> 00:03:03.920
"Blah blah blah, a typical Taurus."

00:03:03.920 --> 00:03:09.520
It's a funny line, but Sheldon's February 26th&nbsp;
birthday makes him a Pisces, not a Taurus.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.520 --> 00:03:15.680
Penny herself even confirms this fact in the&nbsp;
season 8 episode, "The Intimacy Acceleration."

00:03:15.680 --> 00:03:18.880
After learning that it's&nbsp;
Sheldon's birthday, she responds,

00:03:18.880 --> 00:03:22.320
"That is so funny. I would never&nbsp;
have pegged you for a Pisces."

00:03:22.320 --> 00:03:27.760
This might all seem like it's fixating extra hard&nbsp;
on Sheldon's birth date, so to switch things up,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.760 --> 00:03:32.480
have a look at the time the show couldn't&nbsp;
decide where Sheldon was born, instead of when.

00:03:32.480 --> 00:03:37.840
Sheldon's mother, Mary Cooper, became one of The&nbsp;
Big Bang Theory's best-loved supporting characters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.840 --> 00:03:41.920
because of her Texas-sized personality,&nbsp;
and the fact that she and Sheldon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.920 --> 00:03:46.240
are comically different people. One of the&nbsp;
first things that viewers learn about Mary&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.240 --> 00:03:51.040
is that she gave birth to Sheldon in&nbsp;
a rather unconventional location. This&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.040 --> 00:03:55.600
occurs in the episode "The Luminous Fish&nbsp;
Effect," wherein Mary comes to town to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.600 --> 00:04:00.960
try and shake Sheldon out of the depressive&nbsp;
episode he falls into after losing his job.

00:04:00.960 --> 00:04:03.680
While talking to his friends&nbsp;
about her son, Mary says,

00:04:04.240 --> 00:04:05.840
"I'll tell ya, I love the boy to death,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.840 --> 00:04:09.040
but he has been difficult since&nbsp;
he fell out of me at the K-Mart."

00:04:09.040 --> 00:04:13.200
Just one season later, though, viewers&nbsp;
were already given an alternative location&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.200 --> 00:04:18.320
for Sheldon's birth. In the season 2 episode,&nbsp;
"The Lizard-Spock Expansion," Sheldon asserts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.320 --> 00:04:23.040
that he was born at the fictional Lawrence&nbsp;
Memorial Hospital, not at a department store.

00:04:23.040 --> 00:04:26.640
So, after all of that, here's&nbsp;
the lowdown on Sheldon's birth:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.640 --> 00:04:32.400
he was born on February 26 and sometime&nbsp;
in April, between the years 1980-1985,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.960 --> 00:04:37.120
at the K-Mart inside the Lawrence Memorial&nbsp;
Hospital. Glad that's all cleared up!

